  "interpretation_warning": "These are ANNUAL occupancy rates. A winter-dominant property that trades hard Dec-Mar and closes the rest of the year is structurally capped near 25-33% annual occupancy even at 100% winter occupancy. Annual figures for ski prefectures therefore CANNOT be compared with year-round urban occupancy, and a low annual figure is not by itself evidence of weak winter demand. The correct revenue model is winter-season occupancy multiplied by season length, not annual occupancy."
